# CODEOWNERS — workshop placeholders
#
# ⚠️ These are sample team names for educational purposes.
# In a real repo, replace with your own GitHub teams (@your-org/your-team)
# or specific users (@username).
#
# Documentation: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owners for everything — first guard
*                               @BetterDevClub/maintainers

# Agent files — only the team responsible for the pipeline
/.github/agents/**              @BetterDevClub/agent-pipeline-owners
/.claude/agents/**              @BetterDevClub/agent-pipeline-owners
/docs/agent-decisions.md        @BetterDevClub/agent-pipeline-owners

# CI/CD workflows — requires DevOps review
/.github/workflows/**           @BetterDevClub/devops

# Domain model — requires architect review
/src/BookSlot.Domain/**         @BetterDevClub/domain-owners

# Tooling configurations — use caution, impacts everyone
/Directory.*.props              @BetterDevClub/maintainers
/global.json                    @BetterDevClub/maintainers
/.editorconfig                  @BetterDevClub/maintainers

# Architecture tests — only maintainers can modify guardrails
/tests/BookSlot.ArchitectureTests/** @BetterDevClub/maintainers
